 `sendMail` takes MIME (base64, `text/plain`) or a JSON `message`; it keeps a read copy in Sent Items (unless `saveToSentItems` is false) and delivers to each recipient that is a seeded user, without the `Bcc` header.
 
+## Microsoft Graph calendar
+
+Events live in the user's one calendar. Times are UTC: requests give them with `timeZone: "UTC"` (others are refused), and responses give them so, as with `Prefer: outlook.timezone="UTC"`. A series' `recurrence` may follow a `daily`, `weekly`, `absoluteMonthly` or `absoluteYearly` pattern, over an `endDate`, `numbered` or `noEnd` range (expanded three years ahead). Changing or deleting one of its occurrences, by the occurrence's id, makes an exception of it.
+
+`calendarView` lists the events overlapping `startDateTime`–`endDateTime`, series as their occurrences and exceptions. Its `delta` lists them, then, from its `@odata.deltaLink`, those changed since, and as `@removed` those deleted, cancelled or moved out of the window. An unknown delta token answers 410 `SyncStateNotFound`.
+
 ## Seed Configuration
 
